Today topic :- 
1. Architecture design of URL shortner (Bit.ly)

### URL shortner 
- URL shortner like bit.ly which takes the URL and return the shorter size of the URL. Ex
www.example.com/add/user/userId=3&userName=Aditya -> www.bitly/qwd12
- UseCase of this service :- where we have words constraints for the url, so when the user click this url www.bitly/qwd12 the he internally clone to this url www.example.com/add/user/userId=3&userName=Aditya.

- So we will be learning this lecture as Interview based. So HLD interview is always open Ended Question -> expected to ask the question and minimized the constraints. 

### What would be the basic solution or What will our service will be doing? 
1. First thing that our url Shortner will be doing?
 - It has the long url.
 - Then this url is passed to our service where design that how the Long url will be converted into Short Url. 
 - After this, We got the short url.

2. Second thing that our url Shortner will be doing?
 - When we click on the short url 
 - Then the broswer will redirect to the long url

### Questioning more for the requirement gathering. 

1. How many people we are targeting?
 - So let's we have asked that our shortner should be able to generate 20 millions URL a day.

2. Example for generating short URL. 
 - Long URL : www.example.com/add/user/userId=3&userName=Aditya  Convert to www.bitly/qwd12.

3. How small the short url would be? 
 - As short as possible , so this type of question is not have any exact answer like 5,4,6 etc (the letter after our company name like www.bitly/qwd12 has 5 character(qwd12)) 

4. What characters I can use to create a short URL? 
 - Lets say we got to use charaters are 0-9 , a-z, A-Z. 

Flow Discussion -> For the ourselves and for the client/interviewer
 1. User comes to our service by giving us a long url
 2. We will give him back a short URL
 3. User put this short url on the broswer and is redirected to LongURl

 2 task :- 
 1. sort url generation
 2. user redirect

 - So we have created the task on the basis of Flow we discussed. 

5. Back of the envelope calculations ? 
 - To find idea of scale of your application -> About all coming request on server, query per second ? and storage unit? will be calculated. 
 - So no Interviwer will be directly asking for the Back of the envelope calculations, we should analyze by ourselves. 
  
  QPS? 
   - 20 million URL generated per day -> If the service will be generating amount of url then it must be storing this Information daily.  So we have 20 millions call then 20 millions time our database have been Qurried. 
   
   Write Operations  : 20 millions per day 
    Write operation per second : 
     - 20 * 2^20 / 86400 = 231.48 * 10^-6 * 2^20 (changing 10^-6 into this 2^20 )
     - 231 * 2^-20 * 2^20 
     - ~ 231 operations/second

   Read Opertaions : 
   - Generally agar ek baar shor uel generate ho jaaye then uske bahut saare application like storing in some where, or share with some where -> Read opertions bahaut baar ho sakte hai. 
   - So jitni baar bhi us short url par koi click karega utani baar hamare service mai read query aayegi. 
   - Let's take ratio which represent write:Read like 1 : 10  it means ki 10 times jayda read operation ho raha then write operation. 
    Read Operations/sec = WQPS * 10 = 231 * 10 = 2310/sec

   Storage Unit :- 
   - We take the assumption about how long this service will be running. So we ssuming for the 5 years :- 
    - 20 millions URL daily
    - 20 millions * 365 days * 5 years
    - 36500 millions(2^20) records
    - 36.5 * 10^3 * 2^20 records
    - 36.5 * 2^10 * 2^20 records (10^3 = 2^10)
    - 36.5 * 2^30 = 36.5 billions

   - Assume 1 record = 100 byte
   - 35.5 Billion * 100 byte
   - 36.5 * 2^30 * 0.1*10^3 -> 36.5 * 2^30 * 2^10 -> 3.65 * 2^40 -> 3.65 TeraByte Approx

## Steps we would take to do architectural design of the application.
- Client :- A client should exist who request/interacts with the service.
- service/server :- Service which process the request and returns the response. 
- So we are saying that client-server are communicating/interacting with each other, How they interacting, using some Api End point.So we need to discribe that which of the api are uses and what are they doing in the service :- 
 1. Generate a short URL
 2. Redirect to long URL

 - So we need to make two api and their work is mentioned above.

### Dicussing api end point 
1. Generate a short URL :- 
  - So firstly user have the post req  
  How the long URL has been given to server? 
  1. qurey parameter : In key value format like longUrl : value -> are the long url 
    - main url : post : www.bit.ly/api/v1/generate
    - QP : key-value
  2. url ke through de sakta hai : req : www.bit.ly/api/v1/generate/{{longUrl}}
  3. body : json format mai de sakte hai
      - post : www.bit.ly/api/v1/generate
      - body: { }

  - url ke through :- Very bad way to give the LongURL because every broswer has some limts -> If hit the limit then this API will not run on the broswer. 
  - qurey parameter is better then the above method In this main api will be small and Query parameter mai badi value aa sakti hai. -> Here to we can reach the limit. 

  - The best way to do post call is passing through Body. 
    1. Call the api
    2. And pass the long url in the body

  - #### 1. Generate a short URL : 
    POST : www.bit.ly/api/v1/generate
    Body : {longURL}

    return shortURL

2. Redirect to Long URL:- 
  - Here user, put these short url on the broswer then it do the get call
    GET : www.bit.ly/{{shortUrl}}
  -  and the we have to redirect to longUrl

  - #### Redirect to Long URL : 
    GET : GET : www.bit.ly/{{shortUrl}}
    reponse : Redirect to long URL


2. How to Redirect the LongUrl? 
  - We have the short Url, and we browse it on google
  - Then behind the seen this URL go to the Our-service that is bit.ly
  - Then this service will be asked to database for the Long Url
  - Then DB response back to the service 
  - Then service return its response back to broswer/client, 
    - We do not want that our service will just response back to client we want to redirect this url. For this we use status 301 and 302. 

  - Both 301 and 302, status code are responsible for the redirection. So if we have this code then our broswer understand that we have to just redirect the URL. 
   - 301 : Permanenet Redirection :- Broswer understand that the short url is permanently moves to this longUrl. Then Broswer store this LongUrl to the Cache. Now if we click on the shorturl then it will directly uses the Long-Url. -> Client-side Caching ho gaya.
   - 302 : Temporary redirection. Then Broswer understand that we wnating that whenever any client click this ShortURl then it internally comes to our website then we process the ShortDB and return back to the Broswer and then redirection ho. 

   How do we decide to use status code between 301 and 302?
   - If use 301 then user will never come to our service again if the broswer caching is done. Without our service Interferance. It will be good when server is small and we want that to minimize the DB Read Query. So when our application is small and not that optimized. 
    - Disadvantage :- We will never know that how much UserBase uses our website-> we have not any metric system to measure. 

   - If use the 302 then user first come to our service and then we redirect. We do this when server is scalable and the DB Read Query is Optimized. 
   Advantage : We can have the User Matrics. 

   -> If we asked and give this resoning for the status code to interviewer answered to use the 302 status code. 

## Design an Initial Flow :-  